<title>USA: Xerox completes unit sale to Fremont.</title>
<headline>Xerox completes unit sale to Fremont.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xerox Corp said on Friday it completed  the sale of Industrial Indemnity Holdings Inc, a Talegen Holdings  Inc subsidiary, to Fremont Indemnity Co, a unit of Fremont General  Corp.</p>
<p>The purchase price was $365 million in cash and the repayment of $79  million in debt, the company said in a news release.</p>
<p>Industrial Indemnity provides workers compensation coverage and risk  management services, primarily in the western United States.</p>
<p>Xerox said the sale was part of its strategy to disengage from financial  services.</p>
</text>
